# When a human must decide

The changes in this project that an agent must never wave through on its own, however small
the diff looks. The planning stage reads this before self-approving a plan, and the build
stage before skipping the code review. See [`README.md`](README.md) for the gates
themselves.

This file is yours. The installer writes it once and never touches it again, so nothing
here is lost when the template is upgraded.

[Both stages already refuse on the usual grounds — auth, secrets, money, migrations, public
interfaces, dependencies, CI and deploy config. This is for what is particular to *this*
project: the module everyone gets wrong, the file whose format something downstream parses,
the threshold that fails silently, the config a customer depends on. Say why, so the agent
recognises a case you did not list. Delete this paragraph as you fill the list in.]

- **`path/to/thing`.** [What goes wrong, and why the test suite would not catch it.]
